@copilot Simplify AkkaHttpParsingErrorSingletons.endSpan in this existing PR by removing the try/finally around response customization and instrumenter.end. Update this PR directly, not a separate PR.

Use the straightforward sequence already used by PekkoHttpParsingErrorSingletons: close the scope, recover the state, customize the response when non-null, call instrumenter.end with the resulting response and the original handler error, then return the response. Keep this change surgical. AgentInstaller.addHttpServerResponseCustomizers already catches and logs exceptions from each HttpServerResponseCustomizer extension callback. The finally was additional defensive protection for immutable-response rebuilding, but no concrete supported failure case has been identified, and the user chose the simpler Pekko-aligned sequence. Do not add replacement catches, wrappers, tests for hypothetical response-rebuilding failures, or unrelated changes.

Preserve explicit Context.root() parenting, rejection-marker consumption, sampling, the handler's normal and exceptional exit behavior, nullable responses, shared response customization, and all existing tests. Keep the Akka HTTP 10.2+ parser-rejection boundary and older-version instrumentation compatibility unchanged. Do not modify Pekko or address failed-entry state ownership here. Apply the narrowest relevant formatting and run the focused existing Java-route regression tests.

